{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"1. **All 13 consensus items are addressed.** The revised contracts, phases, tests, and end conditions agree on the public VM integration, opaque entries, two-function resolver, terminal writer `closed`, diagnostic handling, complete ordered sweeps, per-call results, and host-owned cadence. The probe section includes all R4 qualifications: terminal retirement, independent pending-write cadence, cursor-state isolation, and “non-advancing” terminology.\n\n2. **Both judgment calls are acceptable.**\n   - Keeping `dao.stream.serving/step!` on host cadence preserves its endpoint maintenance and ordering (`serving.cljc:330`). The proposed non-VM adoption site is valid: `yin.repl.serve/session-step` explicitly prioritizes pending responses over request reads (`serve.cljc:586`), and W4 preserves that priority while replacing unconditional request polling with probes.\n   - `:dao.stream.waitset/unsupported-reason` clearly identifies a library diagnostic without expanding DaoStream’s outcome vocabulary. W2 requires it to raise before continuation restoration.\n\n3. **W0 preservation is verified.** All 21 table lines—including headers and separators—are byte-for-byte identical to the committed census. The reconciliation note is acceptable: it preserves the historical record and explicitly gives the revised sections precedence. W4 supplies the definitive adoption assignments.\n\n4. **The plan is internally consistent and implementable at the architectural level.** No remaining consensus/phase contradiction blocks implementation. Host-owned tick storage is compatible with the prohibition on a library-owned shared state container; the driver receives no interpreter results. Implementation must still satisfy the specified cross-host tests, particularly probe lifecycle, pending writes, and non-reentrant nudges.\n\nNo files were edited.\n\nSIGN-OFF: granted — The revised plan faithfully incorporates the consensus and probe qualifications, preserves the signed census, and provides a coherent implementation contract."}}
